-- the bond beyond second order. In units of L/280, less the common 82, with s = (280 t/L)²: the nuclei at 4 and 9
-- have total energy the lowest root x_f of p_f(x) = x(x − 118)(x − 140) − s(6x − 280) (the three classes of
-- vertices, where the lowest state lies); the nuclei at 4 and 5 have total energy at most the lowest root x_n of
-- p_n(x) = x(x − 88)(x − 128) − s(3x − 344) (the state held to the two nuclei, their shared neighbour and their two
-- other neighbours). p_n − p_f = x(42x − 5256) + s(3x + 64) (`hp-diff`), positive for −64/3 < x < 0, so there
-- p_n(x_f) > 0, and since p_n(0) = 344 s > 0 that puts x_f above x_n. x_f > −64/3 exactly when p_f(−64/3) < 0,
-- which is 27 · 408 · s < 64 · 418 · 484; s = 1156 (t = 34 L/280) satisfies it. So for every t up to 34 L/280 the
-- nuclei sharing a neighbour lie lower than the opposite ones.
hp-bond-range : (if al-id 2 hp-diff then bin-leb (bin-mul (bin-of-nat 1156) (bin-mul (bin-of-nat 27) (bin-of-nat 408))) (bin-mul (bin-of-nat 64) (bin-mul (bin-of-nat 418) (bin-of-nat 484))) else false) ≡ true
hp-bond-range = λ i → true
